From 7ae8459d0f17b7111ce83c050cf30acafc26a5b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yibo Wang <2024312277@stu.hit.edu.cn>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 09:24:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 51/79] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali: asymmetric CPU capacity
 from the vendor calibration

All eight Oryon CPUs carried the 1024 placeholder, hiding the
6+2 cluster asymmetry from the scheduler. Take the vendor
calibration: mid cluster (cpu0-5) capacity-dmips-mhz 1792 and
dynamic-power-coefficient 238, prime cluster (cpu6-7) 1894 and 588.

Verified on the device: cpu_capacity scales to 799 (mid) / 1024
(prime) per the 3.63/4.40 GHz policy maxima, and energy models
register for both clusters, so EAS sees the real asymmetry.

(cherry picked from commit cb23870f29a2baf8ab7d021614e7ca86264056db)
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi | 24 ++++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
index 631dc02da750629cf7399f9e8baa57ad00ed423c..1d2588cd5588f97aac5e7ebc670c611cd80c745a 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
@@ -45,7 +45,8 @@ cpu0: cpu@0 {
 			compatible = "qcom,oryon";
 			reg = <0x0 0x0>;
 			enable-method = "psci";
-			capacity-dmips-mhz = <1024>;
+			capacity-dmips-mhz = <1792>;
+			dynamic-power-coefficient = <238>;
 			d-cache-size = <0x10000>;
 			d-cache-line-size = <64>;
 			d-cache-sets = <256>;
@@ -72,7 +73,8 @@ cpu1: cpu@100 {
